4	
5	## 3. The way built, and why
6	
7	I built way 1. It is the only way that is at once local to the loader, independent of the source path and independent of the order of loading. It rests on the specification's own rule for components: each has a unique name. The other ways fall short:
8	- Way 4 is the strongest identity, but it leans on three facts outside the loader.
9	- Way 2 depends on the path.
10	- Way 3 costs a scan and a new accessor for the same trust as way 1.
11	- Way 5 does not work at load.
12	- Ways 6 to 8 do not identify the declaration.
13	
14	The shadow's code (`StaticNativeApp.java:102-136` in the shadow):
15	
16	    static Class<?> javaForSelf(FType t) {
17	        String n = t.getName();
18	        if (n != null && n.equals("FlatString"))
19	            return FLAT_STRING_COMPONENT.equals(declaringComponent(t)) ? String.class : null;
20	        return javaForSelf(n);
21	    }
22	    static String declaringComponent(FType t) {
23	        if (!(t instanceof FTraitOrObjectOrGeneric)) return null;
24	        Environment e = ((FTraitOrObjectOrGeneric) t).getWithin();
25	        if (e == null) return null;
26	        try {
27	            HasAt at = (e.isTopLevel() ? e : e.getTopLevel()).getAt();
28	            return at instanceof Component ? NodeUtil.nameString(((Component) at).getName()) : null;
29	        } catch (RuntimeException x) { return null; }   // an environment with no top level
30	    }
31	
32	- `javaForSelf(String)`, the table by name, is unchanged. So `JavaString` still carries no `self`: walk's library declares no `JavaString` (only `CompilerBuiltin.fsi:52` does).
33	- The refusal message is unchanged and still names the type (`StaticNativeApp.java:181` in the shadow).
34	
35	**The moved binding** is `size`, because every program reaches it: `||` reads `self.size` (`Library/FlatString.fss:123`, `:134`), and so does `javaSubstr(lo)` (`:91`). Its helper `nativeStrlen` answers `s.length()`, as `FlatString$Size` does (`interpreter/glue/prim/FlatString.java:124-129`). No helper had to be added.
